    <string name="tut_waiting">The bots are moving. Watch the log and the board — every suggestion they make is a clue.</string>
    <string name="rules_win_t">1. How to win</string>
    <string name="rules_win" formatted="false">• Detective — a correct Final Accusation (Suspect + Location + Item in the envelope): instant win.\n• Economic — every opponent bankrupt, or (5–6 players) your wealth ≥ 65% of the table when a Front is revealed.\n• May 1945 Score — if the last Front opens with no winner, the highest score wins.</string>
    <string name="rules_setup_t">2. Setup</string>
    <string name="rules_setup">The envelope holds 1 random Suspect, Location and Item. The rest are dealt evenly; leftovers lie open at the Embassy. Each player: 1,500 escudos, 1 Intel, 1 Tactic card, a faction and a Secret Mission. 3 City Operations open.</string>
    <string name="rules_turn_t">3. Your turn</string>
    <string name="rules_turn">Move → Tile action → Investigate → Business.\nRoll 2 dice (doubles = again, third doubles = Prison) or ride one of your Escape Routes. Resolve the tile. On your own property you may make a suggestion (1 Intel). Then build, mortgage, trade, play 1 Tactic, end your turn.\nPassing START: salary, +1 Intel, −1 Suspicion, +1 Tactic card.</string>
    <string name="rules_economy_t">4. Economy</string>
    <string name="rules_economy" formatted="false">6 districts × 3 properties + 4 Escape Routes. A full district = Spy Cell (base rent ×2, may build). Build evenly: 1–4 Safe Houses then an HQ. Rent ≤ 300 may be paid with information (max 2× per Clock step). Mortgage for half price, redeem +10%.</string>
    <string name="rules_mystery_t">5. The mystery</string>
    <string name="rules_mystery">Suggestion: name Suspect + Item + Location; players are asked clockwise and the first who holds one must show it secretly — or stay silent (1 Intel). Final Accusations open from Clock step 10 and cost 2 Intel. Wrong = Burned. The Red Folder moves at steps 5, 8, 10, 11: one category is redealt!</string>
    <string name="rules_war_t">6. The War Clock</string>
    <string name="rules_war">The Clock advances every ~5 START passes (all players). Each step reveals that month\'s Front (Jun 1944 → May 1945) with immediate effects. The poorest player receives Allied Aid with each new Front.</string>
    <string name="rules_intel_t">7. Intel &amp; Suspicion</string>
    <string name="rules_intel">Intel (max 4) comes from START, Decoding, the Neutral Contact, cards and Operations; spend it on suggestions, silence and accusations. Suspicion 0–6 rises from the Black Market, Casino wins, the PIDE Patrol and enemy Tactics. Reaching 6 = arrested.</string>
    <string name="rules_extras_t">8. Tactics, Operations, Factions</string>
    <string name="rules_extras">24 Tactic cards (Disguise, Sabotage, Blackmail, …) — max 1 per turn. 3 City Operations are always open; the first to meet one earns money, Intel and Prestige. 8 factions with unique abilities — see the Glossary.</string>
    <string name="rules_score_t">9. May 1945 Score</string>
    <string name="rules_score">Money ÷ 10 · property price ÷ 10 (mortgaged half) · Safe House 5 · HQ 25 · Secret Mission · Prestige · End Guess 50 per correct card. Burned ×0.5.</string>
    <string name="rules_modes_t">10. Modes</string>
    <string name="rules_modes">Standard (~4 h) · Quick (starts at Front 5, 2 starting properties) · Family (no Casino/Black Market, wrong accusations fined without Burning) · Campaign (preset starting properties) · Double Agent variant (5–6 players).</string>
</resources>
